+# Certification & Traceability Runbook Template
+
+Purpose
+-------
Guide to produce artifacts required by auditors and map Aegis evidence to certification requirements (ISO 26262 / UNECE R155).
+
+Steps
+1. Requirements listing
+   - Populate ops/certification/requirements.json with structured requirement objects: id, description, owner, criticality.
+2. Evidence ingestion
+   - Ensure CI uploads signed artifacts to evidence store and index (s3 + /tmp/evidence_index.json)
+3. Traceability matrix
+   - Run: python ops/certification/traceability_matrix.py
+   - Review /tmp/traceability_matrix.json and iterate until each requirement has linked evidence.
+4. Mock audit
+   - Produce audit bundle: all evidence referenced in the matrix, plus readme and SME signoffs.
+   - Run internal mock audit and document gaps.
+5. Close gaps
+   - Create GitHub issues for missing evidence, missing SME signoffs or missing HIL runs.
+
+Acceptance
+- Every requirement has at least one signed evidence artifact linked.
+- SME signoff present for safety-critical invariants.
+- HIL/WCET reports for timing requirements are present and signed.
+
